ithin the $750 monthly budget at $527.07. Right-sizing from db.t3.micro to db.t3.medium ($24.82 to $99.28 Multi-AZ) accommodates growth while ElastiCache ($99.28) prevents over-provisioning the database. Using t3.medium instances ($60.74 baseline + $9.98 peak hours) instead of larger instance types minimizes compute costs while meeting capacity requirements. The architecture scales to six instances only during 60 peak hours monthly, avoiding continuous over-provisioning. Single NAT Gateway ($32.85 + $2.25 data) balances cost against the marginal availability gain of multi-AZ NAT. CloudFront ($170 + $40) efficiently serves 50% of requests from cache, reducing origin load and data transfer costs. The 7-day backup retention balances recovery capability with storage costs.\n\n**Sustainability**: Auto Scaling eliminates idle capacity by scaling down to two instances during 670 hours of normal load, reducing energy consumption by 67% compared to continuously running six instances. ElastiCache reduces database query volume and associated compute. CloudFront edge caching reduces long-distance data transfer and origin compute. Right-sized instance types (t3.medium vs. over-provisioned larger instances) minimize resource waste while meeting performance requirements. The architecture provisions capacity to actual demand patterns rather than peak load continuously.",
