pacity per instance, supporting peak promotional loads. ElastiCache reduces database queries by 60-80% for repeated reads, lowering RDS load and improving response times. CloudFront's 50% cache hit rate reduces origin load by half. The architecture can scale to 6 instances in minutes via Auto Scaling, handling traffic spikes. S3 provides unlimited scalability for photo storage with 11 nines durability.\n\n**Cost Optimization**: The proposed architecture costs $748.95 monthly, within the $750 budget (N5). Key optimizations include: right-sizing RDS to db.t3.micro (adequate for reduced load via caching), reducing ALB LCUs from 2 to 1 through efficient request handling, reducing NAT Gateway data transfer via caching (100 GB to 80 GB), running minimum instances (2) during off-peak, and leveraging ElastiCache to defer expensive RDS scaling. The original architecture at $205.09 cannot meet N1 (peak load) or N3 (RPO/RTO requirements) without these investments.\n\n**Sustainability**: Graviton instances were evaluated but t3.medium provides better cost-performance for this budget. ElastiCache reduces redundant database queries, lowering compute waste. CloudFront edge caching reduces data transfer distances and origin compute requirements. Auto Scaling ensures capacity matches demand, avoiding over-provisioning.\n\nThe architecture meets all stated requirements: N1 (750 RPS peak capacity with 960 RPS maximum), N2 (HA via Multi-AZ and minimum 2 instances in 2 AZs), N3 (5-minute RPO via point-in-time recovery, 1-hour RTO via Multi-AZ failover), N4 (CloudFront costs included), N5 ($748.95 under $750 budget), and N6 (EC2 Auto Scaling retained with t3.medium instances).",
